{"id":"s4.5.2","slug":"repeating-decimals-in-reverse","title":"Repeating Decimals in Reverse","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">These problems give you a fraction and ask for the first few digits of its decimal representation. This requires working the repeating decimal formulas in reverse.</p><p class=\"mb-4\">For a fraction like $\\frac{23}{90}$, you know the denominator 90 corresponds to a decimal of the form $.abbb...$. You need to find digits $a$ and $b$ such that the two-digit number $ab - a = 23$. It's quick to see that $25 - 2 = 23$, so the decimal is $.2555...$.</p><p class=\"mb-4\">If the fraction has been reduced (e.g., $\\frac{17}{45}$), you must first un-reduce it to a denominator of 90, 99, 990, etc. In this case, $\\frac{17}{45} = \\frac{34}{90}$. Then solve $ab - a = 34$, which gives $ab=37$. The decimal is $.3777...$.</p>","summary":"These problems give you a fraction and ask for the first few digits of its decimal representation.","generation_guideline":"Generate a problem giving a fraction with a denominator of 90, 99, or a multiple, and ask for the first few digits of its decimal form.","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"The first four digits of the decimal for 16/90 is 0.","answer":"1777","kind":"exact","tags":["repeating-decimals"]},{"id":2,"text":"The first 3 digits of 13/33 is 0.","answer":"393","kind":"exact","tags":["repeating-decimals"]},{"id":3,"text":"The first four digits of the decimal for 17/45 is 0.","answer":"3777","kind":"exact","tags":["repeating-decimals"]},{"id":4,"text":"The first four digits of the decimal for 17/90 is 0.","answer":"1888","kind":"exact","tags":["repeating-decimals"]},{"id":5,"text":"The first 4 digits of the decimal of 43/90 is 0.","answer":"4777","kind":"exact","tags":["repeating-decimals"]},{"id":6,"text":"The first four digits of the decimal for 11/45 is 0.","answer":"2444","kind":"exact","tags":["repeating-decimals"]},{"id":7,"text":"The first 4 digits of 31/90 is 0.","answer":"3444","kind":"exact","tags":["repeating